## Build movement into the design

Spinner challenge coins combine a fixed coin body with a separate element that rotates on an axis. A globe, propeller, emblem or other moving feature brings interaction to collector editions, unit keepsakes and recognition programs without losing the familiar coin format.

## Internal or floating spinner

An internal spinner sits within an opening in the coin body, framed by the surrounding artwork. A floating spinner sits above the face, making movement the central feature. Choose the arrangement around the artwork rather than adding it after the design is complete.

Keep essential lettering clear of the moving connection. The body establishes the stable identity, while the rotating element can reveal a second symbol, message or contrasting face. Coordinate their plating and color so both parts feel like one composition.

## Two components, one finished piece

The coin body and spinner are made separately with their own tooling, then finished and assembled. Tooling for both components is included in the quotation. Each assembled coin is checked for smooth rotation and surface quality before packaging.

## Plan your order

The minimum order is 50 pieces. Typical production takes 14-18 business days, excluding shipping. Send your artwork, dimensions, quantity, delivery country and target date. Explain which part should rotate and what should remain on the fixed frame; edge and packaging choices can be refined during review.
